      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `hash` console command won\u0027t exercise the problematic handling of sub-block sizes because it always calls `SHA256_update` with 512-bit blocks except for the last one.\n\nI believe this would be incorrect:\n```\nSHA256_update(ctx, \"abcd\", 4); // Update with less than a whole block\nSHA256_update(ctx, \"efgh\", 4); // Followed by another update\nSHA256_final(ctx);\n```\n\n..because the result would not be equal to `SHA256(\"abcdefgh\")`.",
